<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Wacom_tablets_and_pressure_sensitivity">Wacom tablets and pressure sensitivity</span></h2>
<p>I finally found time to corner a level artist today, and I'm afraid there's bad news. The toolset doesn't do anything with tablet pressure level input. Sorry.&#160;:( <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20BryanDerksen" title="User:BryanDerksen">BryanDerksen</a> 20:54, 10 November 2009 (UTC)
</p>
<dl><dd>Nooooooo!  *collapses in a sobbing heap*  Ah well, would have been nice, but the configuration I have right now is working rather well.  Thanks for finding out for me&#160;:) <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20Languard" title="User:Languard">Languard</a> 23:09, 10 November 2009 (UTC)</dd></dl>
<dl><dd><dl><dd> Not to get your hopes up without merit, but if you want to delve into the guts of the interface and see if you can fine-tune things even more to your liking, check out Dragon Age\Toolset\DefaultSettings.xml. It's a monster huge XML file that configures all sorts of things for the toolset that there isn't a GUI for in the toolset itself. Just make sure to make a backup copy before you try anything, it's a gigantic file and you can probably break the toolset quite thoroughly with some of the things you can do in there.&#160;:) <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20BryanDerksen" title="User:BryanDerksen">BryanDerksen</a> 03:35, 11 November 2009 (UTC)</dd></dl></dd></dl>
<dl><dd>OK, so before I go and write an app to allow people to configure key bindings, is there already a way to change key-bindings in the editor?  If there is, I haven't seen it.  That file is awesome.  So many cool features exposed.  So much danger of nuking my install&#160;;)  Unfortunately the one feature that I would want exposed, a command to control brush strength, is not there.  But at least I can make my camera move faster now.  Thanks much for pointing this out&#160;:) <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20Languard" title="User:Languard">Languard</a> 05:40, 11 November 2009 (UTC)</dd></dl>
<dl><dd><dl><dd>Not that I'm aware of, beyond whatever's in the "options" pane. <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/User%20-%20BryanDerksen" title="User:BryanDerksen">BryanDerksen</a> 02:50, 13 November 2009 (UTC)</dd></dl></dd></dl>
